  "uprn": "100023404297",
  "decision_date": "24/08/2005",
  "description": "Installation of a synthetic all-weather grass pitch to replace an existing pitch.",
  "site_name": "Heathland School, 460",
  "last_updated_by": "Northgate M3",
  "decision_target_date": "05/05/2005",
  "borough": "Hounslow",
  "postcode": null,
  "street_name": null,
  "bo_system": "Northgate M3",
  "development_type": "Minor retail and service",
  "lapsed_date": "24/08/2005",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - Subject to the appropriate safeguarding conditions, it is not considered that the proposed installation of a synthetic all-weather grass pitch to replace an existing pitch, would harm the appearance of the area, the openness of the Green Belt or result in harm to neighbours' living conditions. The proposal therefore accords with adopted Unitary Development Plan policies ENV-N.1.2 (Acceptable development in the Green Belt) and ENV-B.1.1 (New development).",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 3 - The floodlighting, hereby permitted, shall not be operated outside the hours of 8am to 10pm.",
    "Condition : 4 - Details of lux levels, direction and screening of any floodlighting shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the use of the pitch commences.  Development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details.",
    "Condition : 5 - No development shall take place until full details of both hard and soft landscape works have been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. These works shall be carried out as approved and shall include full details of pitch construction and surfacing. Soft landscape works shall include planting plans, written specifications and an implementation and management program.",
    "Condition : 6 - The access gate to the sports pitch shall have a minimum clear width of 900mm, a level surface or ramp between the path and the pitch and a handle of not more than 1m above ground level."
  ],
